    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d122">

                <pb facs="0292" n="178" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg178"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/4205: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Belgium</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-30T12:00:00+01:00">June 30,
                        1931—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received June 30—9:35 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>63. Reference is to my telegram No. 62 of June 29, 8 p.m.<anchor n="64"
                        xml:id="d122-f1"/> In the event that we need Belgian support for further
                    steps, it will be helpful to me, and my hand will be strengthened if the
                    Department can send an acknowledgment of the Belgian reply in the warmest
                    possible terms. The Belgian Cabinet has run some considerable risk in making a
                    favorable reply before the French decision is announced, in spite of French
                    pressure, against the desires of public opinion and the press, and with the
                    realization that they will have a fight to face the moment the text of the reply
                    becomes known. If we can do anything <pb facs="0293" n="179" xml:id="pg179"/>
                    without engaging ourselves as to details to support them in general terms it
                    will have genuine value as moral support.</p>
                <p>You can judge the sort of message which will have the desired effect. I would not
                    of course suggest any definite assurances to the Belgians.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
